    digest: "The case study traces poppi’s growth from a founder-led Shark Tank brand to a culturally visible beverage acquired by PepsiCo for $2 billion. Its social strategy consistently sells a feeling before a functional ingredient claim. Founder Allison Ellsworth documented the company journey, creating a narrative that continued as the packaging and distribution scaled. User-generated content is actively encouraged through community rewards, while the poppi University ambassador program gives students products, events and reasons to create inside their own networks. The brand invests in recurring creator relationships and places them inside experiences such as Coachella houses, making the content feel like access to a cultural moment rather than a one-off sponsorship. Partnerships with Love Island, BÉIS and Bubble extend the same colorful, wellness-meets-fun identity into adjacent interests. Across TikTok and Instagram, humor, trends and recognizable packaging help poppi behave like a participant in culture. The strategy works because creator selection, community mechanics, collaborations and visual identity all reinforce the same promise instead of operating as disconnected campaigns.",
